I think if human flourishing is is  living well and so you know maybe a  question we've all asked is what is the  good life what does it mean to live well  and that's a question that philosophers  as well as people like you and me of  that over the centuries right  and so I Aristotle had an interesting  answer to that question Aristotle would  say that people flourish when they  exercise virtue and virtues are things  like wisdom and courage so if you think  of a virtue like courage then  flourishing it happens when you exercise  courage even in the most difficult  circumstances so it's possible to  flourish even if you are going through  something really hard and so I would say  mathematics is actually a vehicle for  helping people flourish so if you think  about what it what it means to do  mathematics you know part of what you're  trying to do in mathematics is seek  truth and in seeking truth you build in  abilities virtues of rigorous thinking  handling ideas well being intellectually  honest if you think about what it means  to play with a puzzle or work with a  math problem you're building in  perseverance which is helping you solve  the next problem even if you don't end  up solving this problem and so  mathematics I would say helps people  flourish
 

